	abstract = {Enterprise Revenue Operations (RevOps) teams increasingly leverage the use of artificial intelligence (AI) agents to query and update customer relationship management systems. However, the assessment of large language model (LLM) agent performance in the RevOps tool ecosystem is difficult because it requires: (i) analytics resilient to pagination over large and denormalized API interfaces, (ii) create/update/delete (CRUD) operations with previews and explicit confirmations for delete operations, and (iii) multi-step workflows over the enterprise CRM schemas. RevOpsBench is a large-scale benchmark for the performance evaluation of LLM agents in the RevOps ecosystem using four leading CRMs: HubSpot, Salesforce, Close, Attio. RevOpsBench comprises 6,100 canonical task examples and 78,350 evaluation traces from 1,487 enterprise end users in 214 firms over 14 months. RevOpsBench also proposes execution-grounded evaluation metrics covering the performance aspects of correctness (Execution Accuracy for scalar, table, chart outputs; State-Delta F1 for write operations), safety (Confirmation Compliance Rate and Action Overreach Rate), as well as the tool usage aspects of tool validity (Trace Validity, latency, and cost). RevOpsBench evaluates the performance of six leading LLMs using a unified verification-aware scaffolding platform; the result shows the difficulty in analytics with heavy aggregation and conditional workflows despite the high validity rate in tool calls. RevOpsBench also conducts an ablation study using the GPT-5.2 LLM; the verified scaffolding platform improves the execution accuracy by 7.7 points over the direct tool calls in the RevOps ecosystem. © 2026 IEEE.},
	type = {Conference paper},
	publication_stage = {Final},
