	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105048635165?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {In dynamic flexible manufacturing system with multiautonomous mobile robot (AMR), online decisions jointly optimize operation sequencing, machine assignment, AMR transport allocation, and conflict-free routing with feasible timing. Stochastic job arrivals and routing conflicts tightly couple scheduling and routing, while realized transport times are fed back to affect downstream start times and resource availability. Limited environment representation and execution-aware feedback hinder stable closed-loop coordination and generalization. This study proposes an environment-aware deep reinforcement learning (EaDRL) algorithm. First, the environment state is represented as an operation-machine-AMR heterogeneous graph, and an edge-aware graph transformer captures structured interactions and resource coupling for integrated scheduling learned by proximal policy optimization. Second, cooperative multi-AMR navigation is learned via multiagent reinforcement learning with a confidence-based automatic curriculum for environment-adaptive training, which adapts task difficulty to improve collision-free coordination and generalization. Experimental results show that EaDRL outperforms baselines in makespan, resource utilization, and related metrics, and generalizes well under diverse dynamic conditions. © 2005-2012 IEEE.},
