	abstract = {Generative AI tools are increasingly used to guide novices through complex industrial tasks. While these tools help workers complete tasks quickly, they often inadvertently introduce the “Execution-Reflection Gap”: users blindly follow AI-generated instructions without understanding the underlying principles. This over-reliance on AI discourages workers from truly learning the skills, inhibiting their growth as skilled workers. To address this issue, we propose PRISM (Post-task Reflection via Intelligent Social Multi-agents) -a multi-agent AI debriefing system. Unlike conventional single-agent chatbots, PRISM incorporates three distinct AI agents: Facilitator, Expert, and Peer. The multi-agent architecture of PRISM encourages proactive reflection and psychological safety, transforming workers from passive AI-users into active “sense-makers” of underlying principles. A user study (N=32) demonstrated that our approach significantly outperforms the single-agent baseline, yielding substantially higher reflection quality (DASH) and a 71.7% improvement in causal reasoning scores. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).},
