	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105049440689?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {The expansion of global e-commerce and smart manufacturing has generated unprecedented demand for scalable, autonomous logistics. Traditional automation, reliant on centralized control architectures, proves insufficient in high-density operational environments. Physical Artificial Intelligence represents the next critical evolution in robotics, embedding real-time learning and autonomous decision-making capabilities directly into physical agents. This chapter presents a comprehensive, multi-layered framework for coordinating robotic fleets within warehouse environments. By leveraging a hybrid methodology that encompasses decentralized coordination, reinforcement learning, swarm intelligence principles, and predictive collision avoidance algorithms, the proposed system addresses the primary bottlenecks of modern supply chains. Ultimately, this chapter highlights how embodied intelligence transforms autonomous logistics, establishing the foundation for fully intelligent, self-optimizing Industry 4.0 ecosystems. Copyright © 2027, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. Copying or distributing in print or electronic forms without written permission of IGI Global Scientific Publishing is prohibited. Use of this chapter to train generative artificial intelligence (AI) technologies is expressly prohibited. The publisher reserves all rights to license its use for generative AI training and machine learning model development.},
