	abstract = {This paper focuses on improving the efficiency of path planning and obstacle avoidance in multi-robot optical communication systems while ensuring the stability of optical links. A Gaussian convolution kernel-based image processing method is proposed to reduce the computational complexity of traditional artificial potential field algorithms in multi-target scenarios, thus enhancing the real-time performance of path planning. To address the issue of local extrema in path planning, a combination of Dijkstra’s algorithm and quadratic programming is introduced to optimize the path, avoiding local extrema and achieving global optimality. Additionally, the concept of multi-robot temporal consistency is proposed to ensure time synchronization of all agents along the optical link direction in a multi-UAV (Unmanned Aerial Vehicle) formation, guaranteeing both the stability of the formation and the reliability of the optical link. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed method significantly improves the stability of optical communication links and achieves efficient obstacle avoidance and path planning in multi-UAV formation tasks. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2027.},
