	abstract = {To address the challenge of high proportion power electronicization in the new power system, a systematic development path needs to be established. This study is based on the practice of Chinese power grid enterprises, integrating macro industry data and enterprise operation data, using descriptive statistics, correlation analysis, and multi-agent simulation modeling to quantitatively diagnose core contradictions such as mismatch between technology supply and system demand, and structural imbalance in the industrial chain. Empirical analysis shows that traditional market driven strategies are difficult to effectively enhance supply chain security and technological autonomy. Therefore, this article constructs a four-dimensional collaborative development model of “strategic management - technological innovation - standard guidance - industrial ecology”, and designs a multi-agent simulation platform to conduct long-term dynamic evaluation of different strategies. Finally, taking the “Yangshan Island Offshore Wind Power Flexible Direct Transmission Project” as a typical case, combined with simulation parameters and engineering data, the significant advantages of the “active ecological construction” strategy in improving localization rate and reducing full life cycle costs were verified. This study provides a decision-making framework that combines theoretical rigor and practical operability for power grid enterprises to coordinate technological development and industrial safety. © 2026 SPIE.},
