	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105024934212?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Multi-Agent Path Finding (MAPF) in dynamic environments such as automated warehouses and intelligent transportation systems requires strong coordination and real-time obstacle avoidance capabilities. Traditional methods suffer from limited scalability and sparse rewards, while reinforcement learning (RL)-based approaches often face low sample efficiency in complex scenarios. This paper proposes a novel MAPF framework that integrates a dynamic waypoint generation module, an improved Hindsight Experience Replay (HER) strategy, and a WQMIX based multi-agent reinforcement learning (MARL) architecture. The dynamic waypoint module generates multi-scale intermediate goals based on real-time obstacle distribution and agent positions, enhancing adaptability to dynamic environments. The improved HER prioritizes waypoints as virtual goals and combines progressive and cooperative reward functions to improve learning efficiency and inter-agent coordination. A curriculum learning strategy is applied to gradually increase task difficulty, further stabilizing the training process. Experimental results in grid-based environments demonstrate that the proposed framework significantly outperforms traditional algorithms and baseline MARL methods in terms of success rate, path efficiency, and obstacle avoidance, providing a scalable solution for real-world MAPF applications. © 2025 SPIE.},
