	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105032071500?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {—Strategic emerging industries are a pivotal driving force for future economic and social development. Knowledge is a core engine of these industries, and it is increasingly seen that a single type of knowledge is insufficient to sustain industrial advancement. To explore this topic, this study constructs a knowledge synergistic diffusion S2K2T R model. Based on this model, the basic reproduction number and equilibrium points are derived, and the stability of the equilibrium points is rigorously verified. Numerical simulations delineate the spatiotemporal evolutionary trends of the foundational model and the dynamic evolutionary patterns based on network topology models. The results indicate that the synergistic contact rate between foundational and emerging knowledge significantly influences the scale of knowledge diffusion. In spatial structures, knowledge explosively propagates from point sources to extensive coverage, with enterprise employees being more likely to be influenced by proximate knowledge dissemination cohorts. An increase in the average degree of the network further facilitates the dissemination of foundational knowledge. Moreover, cross-domain knowledge collisions transcend the boundaries of isolated knowledge systems, accelerate the recombination of heterogeneous knowledge, and increase the likelihood of breakthrough technological innovations. © 2026, International Association of Engineers. All rights reserved.},
