	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105024839590?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {The maritime industry, long considered the backbone of global trade, is undergoing a transformation as digital technologies reshape how ports, vessels, and logistics systems operate. Traditionally reliant on physical infrastructure and manual coordination, maritime operations now integrate cloud computing, edge intelligence, AI, and IoT to enhance efficiency, safety, and sustainability. This chapter explores how these technologies reconfigure maritime infrastructure into data- driven ecosystems enabling real- time coordination and predictive decision- making. It highlights opportunities such as fleet optimization, predictive maintenance, and smarter port operations, while noting challenges like data sovereignty, cybersecurity, and the exclusion of smaller ports. It stresses that successful transformation must extend beyond technology, addressing governance, inclusivity, and human factors. Ultimately, it argues that a resilient and fair "maritime cloud" can bridge oceans, foster collaboration, and sustain the next era of global trade. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.},
