	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105049318462?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {This chapter addresses the core contribution of reinforcement learning (RL) in defining the next generation of artificial intelligence advancement. While artificial intelligence systems are advancing from passive pattern recognition to active interaction with their surroundings and decision-making, RL is considered the paradigm that allows autonomous agents to learn, adapt, and optimize their behaviors through experiential learning. This research addresses the convergence of large-scale foundation models with RL algorithms and how their combination surmounts conventional limitations such as sample efficiency, generalization, and exploration issues. Further, it addresses new paradigms such as multiagent RL, hierarchical learning frameworks, and human-AI cooperative systems, which are revolutionizing the field of intelligent systems. We examine real-world applications in a wide range of domains such as robotics, autonomous technologies, game theory, and decision sciences, without forgetting key issues such as safety, alignment, and ethics. Through an exhaustive review of current research and future advancements, this chapter shows how RL is the underlying technology that facilitates the transition to artificial general intelligence, thereby revolutionizing the way intelligent systems interact with and affect their surroundings. © 2026 Walter de Gruyter GmbH, Genthiner Straße 13, 10785 Berlin, Germany.},
