	abstract = {Sustainability in the commercial fleet is crucial for reducing environmental impact and improving operational efficiency. This study examines the potential benefits of Internet of Things (IoT) technology for sustainability through data-driven decision-making and real-time monitoring. The objectives include lowering carbon emissions, improving fuel efficiency, ensuring compliance with environmental regulations, and enhancing safety. IoT connects devices and systems to monitor fuel use, greenhouse gas emissions, and indoor air quality (IAQ). Advanced sensors lower risks and ensure compliance with environmental standards by giving real-time information on things like temperature management and issuing alerts for hazardous conditions like high CO2 levels or driver fatigue. By integrating IoT, fleet operators may improve driver safety and lower accident rates while cutting expenses, optimizing resource use, and satisfying regulatory requirements. IoT-based IAQ systems, for example, can identify low air quality in driver cabins and initiate preventive measures, such as modifying ventilation or taking breaks, to lower the dangers associated with fatigue. This chapter also looks at how IoT-enabled smart energy management systems can be implemented and evaluates how well they work to improve indoor air quality, lower energy use, and boost customer happiness. IoT technologies can help fleet operators tackle issues like air pollution and fuel inefficiencies while promoting environmental sustainability. © 2026 by Apple Academic Press, Inc.},
