	title = {ORCA-LF: Adaptive Leader-Follower Formation and Distributed Obstacle Avoidance for Ground Robots},
	year = {2025},
	journal = {Proceedings - 2025 IEEE International Symposium on Parallel and Distributed Processing with Applications, ISPA 2025},
	pages = {1006 - 1014},
	doi = {10.1109/ISPA67752.2025.00137},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105030213454?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {In obstacle-rich environments, each agent in a Leader-Follower multi-agent robotic formation faces simultaneous constraints from collision avoidance and formation maintenance, often leading to conflicting requirements. To address this conflict, we introduce an adaptive weighting mechanism that integrates the Optimal Reciprocal Collision Avoidance (ORCA) algorithm with a Leader-Follower formation control model, termed ORCA-LF. This method effectively balances the safety of obstacle avoidance with the stability of formation control. Theoretical analysis demonstrates that in obstacle-free environments, the proposed method guarantees asymptotic convergence of formation errors, while in environments with obstacles, it ensures formation errors remain bounded. Simulation results verify that ORCA-LF, while maintaining distributed control characteristics, effectively balances the demands of collision avoidance safety and formation stability. It demonstrates robustness and practical applicability across various scenarios, including open spaces, dynamic obstacle regions, and narrow passages, thus providing a solid theoretical foundation and technical support for deploying ground-based multi-agent systems in real-world engineering applications.  © 2025 IEEE.},
