	doi = {10.1109/TELEPE66277.2025.00116},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105031427566?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Mobile pressure vessel plays an important role in industrial production, energy supply and public transportation, but its complex working environment and characteristics of dangerous media make safety monitoring the key to ensure its reliable operation. In this paper, an intelligent algorithm and model based on support vector machine (SVM) is proposed for safety monitoring of mobile pressure vessels. The model is constructed by five modules: data preprocessing, feature selection, model training optimization, anomaly detection and model verification. The radial basis function (RBF) kernel function is used to deal with the nonlinear relationship, and the parameters are optimized by grid search and cross verification. In practical application, taking the liquefied natural gas transportation fleet of a logistics company as an example, the data are collected by various sensors and preprocessed and model trained. The results show that the model is superior to the traditional decision tree and random forest algorithm in accuracy (93.2%) and false alarm rate (1.3%), with a response delay of 12.4 ms and excellent performance in resource consumption and anomaly detection. This research provides an efficient and reliable intelligent algorithm and model for the safety monitoring of mobile pressure vessels, which has high practical value and popularization prospect. ©2025 IEEE.},
