	abstract = {This paper presents a multi-agent reinforcement learning (MARL) framework for coordinated industrial automation in Artificial Intelligence of Things (AIoT) environments. The framework addresses challenges in decentralized multi-robot systems, including partial observability, communication constraints, and multi-objective optimization for efficiency, safety, and energy use. We model the system as a multi-agent Markov game with decentralized policy learning, graph-based inter-agent communication, and multi-objective reward shaping, implemented using a multi-agent variant of Proximal Policy Optimization (MAPPO). In a simulated smart warehouse, our system achieves up to 40% faster task completion and 30% lower energy consumption compared to single-agent PPO, MADDPG, and rule-based heuristics. The framework scales to 50 agents while reducing communication overhead by 45%, with emergent cooperative behaviors like dynamic task sharing and congestion avoidance, offering a scalable blueprint for industrial AIoT applications. © 2025 IEEE.},
