	abstract = {Multi-agent reinforcement learning shows great potential in dynamic complex systems, but it still faces challenges in terms of strategy stability and robust planning under uncertainty in competitive scenarios. In this paper, we propose a dynamic competitive deep Q network (DC-DQN) and its uncertainty enhancement variant Dropout-DC-DQN to overcome the shortcomings of traditional methods in strategic coupling effect, environmental noise sensitivity and dynamic competition regulation ability. By integrating adaptive competition reward mechanism, strategy diversity constraint and double randomization network design, the agent can adjust competition intensity flexibly in the game and improve the tolerance to observation noise, dynamic obstacles and other disturbances. Compared with the baseline model, the hunting success rate of DC-DQN increased by 23.1%, the strategy differentiation increased by 216%, the anti-interference index of Dropout-DC-DQN reached 0.93, and the dynamic obstacle avoidance rate increased by 21.4% compared with the traditional method. This study provides a solution with both strategic flexibility and environmental adaptability for scenarios such as autonomous driving cooperation and distributed resource scheduling. © 2025 IEEE.},
