	abstract = {The rapid progression of artificial intelligence and robotics is bringing a transformation to pharmaceutical manufacturing with the potential of fully autonomous, intelligence-based manufacturing systems. This paper presents a holistic framework incorporating multi-agent reinforcement learning for intelligent process planning, AI-based quality inspection, federated learning for secure process control, and digital twins for real-time simulation. This methodology supports adaptable, compliant, and efficient pharmaceutical manufacturing workflows under Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP) regulations. We performed comparative evaluations against existing traditional and semi-automated systems, showing across the sample significant improvement: 93.4 % production efficiency, 97.9 % defect detection accuracy, and a 62.8 % time reduction on downtime. Use cases demonstrate the framework's potential for improving operational resilience, quality assurance, and sustainability. While we have assessed the framework in high-fidelity simulations, we wish to reiterate that the current findings will only be fully realised through deployed and regulated real-world systems. In summary, the AI-robotics system presented offers a fully autonomous and scalable next-generation pharmaceutical manufacturing system that will enable precision, safety, and compliance in the emerging digital health ecosystem. © 2025 IEEE.},
