	abstract = {The path planning of Automated Guided Vehicle (AGV) is a core focus of research in intelligent warehousing, with the primary objective of determining collision-free routes for multiple agents while minimizing total travel distance. Many traditional algorithms have been applied in path planning, such as A*, Enhanced Conflict-Based Search (ECBS), and Prioritized Path Search (PPS). However, these algorithms face several limitations in path planning, including the risk of premature convergence to local optima, high demand for computational resources, and poor adaptability in dynamic environments. To address these issues, a novel Multi-Agent Path Finding with Large Neighborhood Search integrating Diffusion Path and Newton-Raphson Based Optimizer (MLDN) algorithm is proposed for warehouse path planning. The proposed MLDN algorithm enhances the path planning process by combining global exploration with local refinement, leading to improved search efficiency. Simulation experiments validate the effectiveness of the proposed method, showing that the MLDN algorithm outperforms traditional algorithms in path length optimization. © 2025 Technical Committee on Control Theory, Chinese Association of Automation.},
