	abstract = {To address the challenges of formation maintenance and cooperative obstacle avoidance for multi-AGV systems in complex warehouse environments, this paper proposes a fuzzyadaptive artificial potential field (Fuzzy-APF) method. Built upon the leader-follower framework, the method introduces dual fuzzy controllers for repulsion weight tuning and offset compensation. By leveraging real-time states including obstacle distance, intervehicle spacing, formation error, and leader trajectory curvature, the controllers adaptively adjust repulsion weights and generate feedforward compensation forces, achieving a dynamic balance between 'rigid maintenance' and 'flexible response.' Simulation results show that, compared with the traditional APF method, the proposed approach significantly suppresses position errors and preserves formation stability in high-speed turning scenarios. In both static and dynamic cooperative obstacle avoidance cases, it produces smoother trajectories and maintains larger internal safety margins. The proposed dual fuzzy-controller framework proves to be a highly effective strategy for dynamically balancing the conflicting objectives of trajectory tracking and safe navigation in complex multi-agent systems. © 2025 IEEE.},
