	abstract = {Predictive maintenance has emerged as the very crucial solution to minimize operating downtime and cost in fleet management. This paper presents DriveSure, an innovative machine learning predictive analytics system that can be used to forecast truck failures, plan maintenance, and enhance overall fleet efficiency. Leveraging multiple datasets like transportation tracking, logistics activity, and large truck fleet data, the system integrates vehicle parameters, maintenance history, and working habits in an attempt to forecast potential failures. The proposed framework employs machine learning algorithms such as random forest, XGBoost, and LSTM networks for encoding structured and time-series relationships in fleet data. The framework addresses three prediction targets: binary classification for probabilities of breakdown in 30 days, regression-based prediction of days to next required maintenance, and multi-class prediction of specific maintenance needs. Experiment results indicate potential business value in the form of 30-50% reduction in unplanned downtime, year-end savings 100K-500K per fleet, and 5-15% fuel efficiency improvement. Proactive maintenance also makes fleets safer through reduced mechanical failures that would otherwise result in accidents. A frontend that is easy to use is created with streamlit that allows for interactive visualization and decision-making by fleet operators. This work focuses on the integration of advanced analytics and real-world logistics data to enable scalable data-driven maintenance strategies that increase operational robustness, safety, and cost-effectiveness in modern-day transportation networks. © 2025 IEEE.},
