	doi = {10.1109/LRA.2025.3620244},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105018867308?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Previous multi-agent deep reinforcement learning (MADRL) algorithms have shown strong performance in symmetric scenarios. However, research on numerically disadvantaged scenarios is limited and challenging. This letter proposes a MADRL algorithm based on collaboration and target assignment for this game scenario. Initially, Markov games (MGs) model is designed. The state space, action space, and reward function of MGs have a significant impact on the performance of MADRL algorithms. Then, to enhance information perception and prevent target omission and resource waste, a novel MADRL algorithm is proposed, named collaboration and target assignment for multi-agent decision-making (CTAMD). The collaboration and target assignment model of CTAMD utilizes graph attention network (GAT) to identify key targets and teammates, forming a new collaboration and target assignment graph (CTG). Building on these CTG features, the multi-agent decision-making model of CTAMD formulates collaboration strategies. Simulation results show that the proposed CTAMD method effectively tackles the multi-agent decision-making challenges in numerically disadvantaged scenarios. It achieves high win rates in various settings. Moreover, It outperforms all baseline algorithms, particularly achieving the highest decision-making efficiency, with the episode length reduced by 62% and the safety-related mean death distance increased by 147%.  © 2016 IEEE.},
