	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105040585653?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {In industrial and civilian settings, the storage environment of safety tools significantly impacts equipment performance and lifespan. Traditional safety tool cabinets face challenges in dehumidification and temperature control, such as inefficient dehumidification, high energy consumption, and uneven environmental conditions. To address these issues, this paper presents an innovative dehumidification and temperature control method for intelligent safety tool cabinets based on multiagent reinforcement learning. The proposed method features a novel Feature Fusion Lightweight Network (FFLN), which integrates multi-dimensional state information from different agents into a unified feature space through a three-layer MLP structure, followed by a lightweight two-layer GRU network for efficient decision-making. This architecture enables precise control of the cabinet environment while significantly reducing system energy consumption. Simulation experiment results demonstrate the effectiveness and feasibility of the proposed strategy, showing improved control accuracy and stability compared to existing methods.  © 2025 IEEE.},
