	title = {SAFE-HGX: A Hierarchical and Safety-Aware Reinforcement Learning Framework for Intrusion Response in Industrial Control Systems},
	year = {2025},
	journal = {2025 1st International Conference on Advancement in Futuristic Technologies, ICAFT 2025},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/ICAFT66710.2025.11453104},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105037325835?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {As advanced persistent threats (APTs) become more sophisticated, intrusion response systems must operate effectively in scenarios characterised by uncertainty and limited resources. This research introduces SAFE-HGX, a hierarchical, safety-oriented multi-agent reinforcement learning (MARL) framework intended for use in Industrial Control Systems (ICS) and Internet of Things (IoT) environments. SAFE-HGX brings together two crucial new ideas: using particular agent roles to break down difficult reaction actions into smaller sections and recurrent state encoding to deal with partial observability while maximising safety-focused rewards. Training uses a mix of offline and online methods. At first, it uses emulation logs to learn policies safely offline. Then, it uses secure real-time adaptation to make the system stronger. Tests done on simulated APT scenarios reveal that SAFE-HGX is substantially superior to baseline DQN and PPO agents in both learning speed and containment accuracy, and it generalises better when time is short. These results show that the framework is good for use in next-generation security operations centres (SOCs) and autonomous defence platforms. © 2025 IEEE.},
