	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105031098114?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {This paper presents a robust approach for collision-free navigation and formation control in multi-agent system (MAS) composed of nonholonomic mobile robot. The proposed method integrates the Improved Artificial Potential Field (IAPF) to avoid the obstacles, and Boids algorithm to achieve rigid coordination in complex environments. Two scenarios (polygon and V-shape) are simulated under environment that contains few obstacle, aim to evaluate the effectiveness of the formation control and obstacle avoidance. All agents will start on random position, then shaped the formation as the time going while achieving the goal coordinates. Results shows that IAPF consistently outperforms the classical Artificial_ Potential Field (APF) by achieving higher order parameters (Ψ > 0.91), faster navigation times (< 35 s), and reliable formation maintenance, even in presence of static obstacles. The agents rapidly each consensus and remains stable formations throughout navigation, while APF method is prone to collisions in cluttered environments. These findings highlight the potential of IAPF framework for real world applications. © 2025 IEEE.},
