	abstract = {Autonomous terrain leveling and material handling operations play a pivotal role in earthworks, directly affecting project timelines, cost efficiency, and environmental impact. We present the Optimal Orchestration Transport Planner Framework (OOTPF), a unified orchestration architecture for multi robot systems that casts surface leveling as an online Multi Agent Pickup and Delivery (MAPD) problem. OOTPF comprises two principal layers: an Optimal Transport layer that formulates material movement via discrete Earth Mover's problems, and a Task Allocation layer that employs heuristic bidding and consensus based auctions to assign pickup-delivery jobs to agents. To guarantee safe, collision free execution, we embed a token driven, priority based planning discipline atop a shared space time Reservation Table, invoking Safe Interval Path Planning (SIPP) for single robot requests and Conflict Based Search (CBS) when multiple robots contend. This hierarchical scheme dynamically balances throughput with conflict resolution. Numerical experiments on representative leveling scenarios demonstrate that OOTPF achieves high utilization, zero collisions, and flexible to import different path planner algorithms.  © 2025 IEEE.},
