	title = {Multi-dimensional Path Design and Simulation for Low-Altitude Economy Development Based on Deep Learning Algorithm},
	year = {2025},
	journal = {2025 7th International Conference on Frontier Technologies of Information and Computer, ICFTIC 2025},
	pages = {1282 - 1287},
	doi = {10.1109/ICFTIC68075.2025.11324458},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105035257801?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {As a national strategic emerging industry, the development of the low-altitude economy involves the synergistic evolution of a multi-dimensional complex system encompassing airspace management, safety assurance, industrial integration, and business model innovation. Traditional planning methods struggle to effectively address the inherent high-dimensional, nonlinear, and dynamic coupling characteristics of this system. To this end, this paper proposes a framework for the design and simulation of multi-dimensional development paths for the low-altitude economy based on a deep learning algorithm. Firstly, a multi-source information fusion indicator system is constructed, integrating airspace physical parameters, real-time operational data, regional economic indicators, and policy texts, providing a data foundation for path design. An Agent-based computational experimental platform is constructed to dynamically simulate and evaluate the development trends of the low-altitude economy under different paths. Simulation results demonstrate that, compared to linear planning paths, the proposed data-driven multi-dimensional path schemes significantly improve key metrics such as economic growth, safety efficiency, and technological innovation, with an average optimization margin of 15%-30%. This research offers an innovative theoretical model and a quantifiable simulation tool for the precise governance and scientific decision-making of the low-altitude economy. © 2025 IEEE.},
	type = {Conference paper},
	publication_stage = {Final},
