	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105041826402?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {In the era of intelligent automation, autonomous decision-making and trajectory optimization in Multi-Robot Systems (MRS) remain pivotal for mission success, particularly in unstructured and dynamic environments. This paper presents a novel hybrid path planning architecture that integrates classical A∗ algorithms with a trainable neural heuristic, forming a differentiable A∗ Neural Network (A∗ NN). Designed for IoTconnected MRS, the system enables decentralized task execution, where object poses, human positions, and obstacle data are shared across a hierarchical communication layer utilizing MQTT broker based messaging. This structure supports scalable data exchange, coordination, and real-time updates between heterogeneous agents, including drones and humanoid robots. The proposed framework leverages sensor fusion from different sensors, visual cameras, and onboard sensors to construct a unified environmental map for navigation and obstacle avoidance. A decentralized data structure is introduced to manage robot states, task conditions, battery levels, and anomaly signals. These parameters drive a learned guidance function that generates heuristic maps dynamically, allowing the A* NN to prioritize efficient, collision-free paths. The network is trained through end-to-end gradient descent to continuously refine decision quality based on real-world feedback. By combining classical path planning with deep learning and decentralized IoT-based communication, the system delivers robust, energy aware, and adaptive navigation performance for mission-critical operations. This work demonstrates a scalable and intelligent solution for real-time decision-making in IoTconnected robotic fleets.  © 2025 IEEE.},
