	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105016842850?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Conflict detection models are fundamental components in MAPF (multi-agent path finding) problems. This paper presents a novel conflict model for the MAPF problem of an AGF (automated guided forklift) system, which coordinates multiple AGFs in space-constrained industrial environments. In real applications, the AGFs' relatively large body sizes and complicated contours make it difficult to apply existing conflict models based on the occupancy model for AGVs (automatic guided vehicles). To operate within densely populated path networks, the conflict relationship between different path segments must be considered, while the existing path segment conflict models may still not sufficiently characterize the conflict relationship between forklifts operating in the real world. We propose a dual conflict model, by taking into consideration the safety trigger logic of AGFs, to represent the forklift traffic control mechanism in space-constrained environments. A complete MAPF algorithm is also developed on the basis of the dual conflict model, whose performance is validated through both simulation and actual field tests.  © 2025 IEEE.},
