	abstract = {This paper presents an LTL-based approach for multi-robot path planning in firefighting environment. Each robot is assigned an LTL task, and the proposed strategy combines offline discrete path planning with online path updates. When resources are insufficient, robots autonomously plan paths to replenish them. Vector-field-based navigation is used to guide robots along the planned discrete paths, while a repulsion force equation is incorporated into the field, enabling robots to avoid collisions with each other. A simulated fire environment demonstrates the approach: robots initially plan their paths and then update their paths to recharge and refill water during movement. After completing the first firefighting task, if a second fire outbreak occurs, the firefighting robots can update their paths and move toward the new fire area. © 2025 IEEE.},
