	abstract = {Cooperative pursuit systems based on traditional model control rules are less adaptable and less robust to complex dynamic environments. In this paper, we study the cooperative pursuit-evasion with collision avoidance in multi-robot systems. We first adopt the Multi-Agent Twin Delayed Deep Deterministic policy gradient (MATD3) algorithm, and design a cooperative pursuit framework that uses the information of multiple robots in the learning process to more accurately predict the actions that robots will take. Then, we propose a Prioritized Experience Replay based MATD3 (PER-MATD3) algorithm which solves the problem of sparse reward in multi-robot cooperative pursuit algorithm by adopting the higher prioritized experience data update network when sampling. Simulation results show that the proposed PER-MATD3 algorithm reduces the collisions among robots, the collisions between robots and obstacles, and the capture time by 60.97%, 68.42%, and 30.37% respectively compared with the baseline algorithms. Moreover, the PER-MATD3 algorithm improves the capture success rate by 25.71% and achieves a faster convergence speed in continuous decision-making than the baseline algorithms.  © 2024 ACM.},
