	abstract = {Cooperative detection of fixed detection sequence positions in complex underwater areas through multi-agent combination is an indispensable means to complete special underwater detection tasks. Studying the scheduling and matching underwater robot resources to meet the requirements of environmental detection tasks under the conditions of meeting task and detection requirements is a research hotspot in the field of multi-agent task allocation. In traditional task allocation process, the detection dimension is single, and the fixed detection sequence is disre garded. This work proposes a novel multidimensional resource scheduling allocation algorithm (CR-C-NSPSO) for heterogeneous agents based on improved NSPSO. The algorithm is composed of a solution set conflict resolution algorithm and a collision optimization strategy module. It can establish a mathematical expression model that meets the needs of a fixed sequence of tasks and builds a solution space for each task while resolving the needs of task conflicts in the same time and space. On the basis of meeting the task priority, the impact of resource scheduling and allocation conflicts caused by optimized search is weakened. Finally, simulations verify the feasibility and effectiveness of the algorithm. © 2022, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd.},
