	abstract = {Hard Time Tasks setting life limits on several critical components used on the Naval Aircrew Common Ejection Seat (NACES) have not yet been determined. This report documents a statistical Weibull analysis using Fleet reported Organizational Level data from the Naval Aviation Logistics Data Analysis (NALDA) system and Martin Baker Aircraft Company, LTD. (MBA) failure data, collected from their Failure Summary and Analysis Reports, on the NACES Barostatic Release Unit (BRU). Weibull Analysis requires life data that is relevant to the failure mode. This analysis does not provide a failure prediction primarily because failure modes within the data could not be segregated. This report recommends collection of appropriate failure data at the component point of repair. It also recommends that both NAVAIRSYSCOM and MBA further consider the Reliability Centered Maintenance default methods as explained in NAVAIR 00-25-403. The methodology discussed in this paper may have wider application to anyone involved in balancing component service life/cost versus reliability/safety.},
